data.reasoningText:
Now I have a good understanding of the project. Let me plan the component decomposition and implement it.

## Component Plan: Settings Dashboard

### Component Tree
```
SettingsPage                    (page — owns active section, orchestrates layout)
├── SettingsSidebar             (vertical nav tabs)
├── ProfileSection              (profile editing form)
├── NotificationsSection        (notification preferences)
├── SecuritySection             (security settings)
│   ├── ChangePasswordPanel     (expandable password change form)
│   └── RevokeSessionDialog     (confirmation dialog)
└── AppearanceSection           (theme/font/language settings with live preview)


```

For the data flow, SettingsPage will manage which section is active, and each section will independently fetch its own data through the ISettingsService since only one is visible at a time. The sidebar receives the active section state and emits changes, while each section component manages its own form state and communicates directly with the service.

I'll start by creating the models and service interface, then build the leaf components like the sidebar and dialogs before moving up to the full sections.

Creating all the files...

Namespace: `sv_e0a9608232cf4e858fc3679f81403fff`

Starting with models and service contracts...

```

csharp
